Subject: [PATCH] [3.14] gh-162282: Fix remaining quadratic paths in
 urllib.robotparser (GH-162442) (#162450)

gh-162282: Fix remaining quadratic paths in urllib.robotparser (GH-162442)

Merging many groups for the same user agent copied the accumulated rule
lines on every merge, and _find_entry() checked a group once per user
agent in it, so a single lookup for an unlisted agent was quadratic in
the number of agents.

Extend a merged entry in place when no other agent shares it, reuse one
merged entry for all agents of a group that shared the same entry, and
check each distinct entry only once in _find_entry().
(cherry picked from commit 06eb74514678a3b1754f3667d0068587c968f0fe)

Co-authored-by: Andrew Svetlov <andrew.svetlov@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
